// Debug build configuration. Used for simulator development
// on the developer's Mac. The iOS simulator can reach the
// Mac's loopback over the shared network namespace, so
// HYLETE_API_SCHEME + HYLETE_API_HOST + HYLETE_API_PATH
// resolves to the local `make dev` server.
//
// A real iPhone cannot reach this address. For on-device
// installs, use a Release build (which picks up
// Release.xcconfig and points at the production server).
//
// Why three variables instead of one? xcconfig treats `//`
// as a line-comment delimiter even inside quoted values, so
// a single `HYLETE_API_BASE_URL = http://localhost...` would
// be truncated to `http:`. Splitting the URL into scheme /
// host / path lets Info.plist concatenate them with
// `://` and `$(HYLETE_API_PATH)` in the middle, where the
// `//` is created at expansion time and never seen by the
// xcconfig parser.
HYLETE_API_SCHEME = http
HYLETE_API_HOST = localhost:8080
HYLETE_API_PATH = /api/v1

// The Debug configuration installs as a SEPARATE app from the
// Release one: a `.dev` bundle ID and a "Hylete Dev" home-screen
// name let a production install and a dev install coexist
// side-by-side on the same device/simulator without overwriting
// each other. iOS sandboxes Keychain per bundle ID, so the two
// apps also keep independent logins.
//
// These deliberately live here and NOT in project.yml's target
// settings — direct build settings in the pbxproj take precedence
// over xcconfig files, which would pin every configuration to a
// single value.
PRODUCT_BUNDLE_IDENTIFIER = com.hyleteapp.hylete.dev
HYLETE_DISPLAY_NAME = Hylete Dev
